# apps/server — copy to `.env` and fill in. NEVER commit a real value.
#
# `DATABASE_URL` — a Neon connection string. Use a DEV BRANCH for migration
# work, not the primary. The sync server never runs a destructive statement, but
# `drizzle-kit migrate` creates tables and a branch is disposable when it does not
# do what you expected.
#
# Read it LAZILY (see src/lib/db/index.ts). A missing or placeholder value does
# NOT break `vite build` — it only fails when a query actually executes, with a
# message that names this variable.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://<user>:<password>@<host>/<db>?sslmode=require"

# `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` — signs session tokens. Generate your own:
#   bun -e 'console.log(crypto.randomUUID() + crypto.randomUUID().replaceAll("-",""))'
# It must be the SAME value across every instance, or tokens minted by one will
# be rejected by another. Treat it as a password: never inline it into a
# Dockerfile, a fly.toml, or a commit.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=""

# `APP_ORIGIN` — the public origin of THIS server, used by Better Auth for its
# own origin checks and for building absolute callback URLs. No trailing slash.
# Local dev: http://localhost:5173
APP_ORIGIN=""

# `TRUSTED_ORIGINS` — comma-separated extra origins allowed to call the auth
# endpoints. Must include the Capacitor WebView origin (`capacitor://localhost`
# on Android) and the Tauri one (`https://localhost` on desktop), plus the
# landing site's origin. Cross-origin cookies are hostile inside a WebView, which
# is why the app authenticates with a bearer token instead — but Better Auth
# still checks the Origin header, so it has to know about them.
TRUSTED_ORIGINS="capacitor://localhost,https://localhost"

# `PORT` / `HOST` — read by adapter-node's `build/index.js`. Fly.io injects PORT.
# PORT=3000
# HOST=0.0.0.0
